<title>INDIA: Yield on Indian 364-day t-bill slips to 12.13 pct.</title>
<headline>Yield on Indian 364-day t-bill slips to 12.13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said it set a cut-off price of 89.21 rupees at its 364-day treasury bills auction on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Traders said the yield worked out to 12.13 percent, down from 12.65 percent at the previous auction.  </p>
<p>The following are the details of Wednesday's auction.</p>
<p>    Bids received (Number)   54</p>
<p>			(Amount)   12.85 billion rupees</p>
<p>    Cut-off price		89.21 rupees</p>
<p>    Bids accepted (number)    4.0</p>
<p>			(Amount)    1.51 billion rupees</p>
<p>    Weighted average price   89.23 rupees</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 900</p>
</text>
